\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Two edges in series}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Take vertices #{0,1,2} and unit edges joining #{0} to #{1}
and #{1} to #{2}. Retain #{\{0,2\}} and eliminate #{1}. The
block off the retained pair is the entry #{2}. The formula of
\ref{fdip-00DH} gives
##{\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}
-\frac{1}{2}\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\1&1\end{pmatrix}
=\frac{1}{2}\begin{pmatrix}1&-1\\-1&1\end{pmatrix}.}
The [kept form](fdip-00DF) of a function #{u} is
#{\frac{1}{2}\bigl(u(0)-u(2)\bigr)^2}. The
[effective conductance](fdip-00DF) between the endpoints is
#{\frac{1}{2}}.}
